he 5th-largest in the Volga Federal District.", "newValue": "Perm, originally known as Yagoshikha and briefly as Molotov, emerged as a significant administrative center in the Russian Empire during the Early Modern period. Founded in 1723 on the banks of the Kama River near the Ural Mountains, it served as a vital hub for the development of the region, particularly in the context of resource extraction and industrialization. The strategic location facilitated trade routes that linked Europe and Asia, making Perm a focal point in the expansion of Russian influence in the East.

